  "description": "\u201cParallelograms which are on equal bases and in the same parallels are equal to one another.\u201d\n\u2014 Euclid's Elements, BOOK I \u2022 PROP. 36 (G.65)\n\n00:00 1 \u00b7 GIVEN: \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9, \u27e8 E F G H \u27e9 (/ B C / = / F G /, / A H / \u2225 / B G /)\n00:21 2 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: segment(B, E) \u2192 / B E /, segment(C, H) \u2192 / C H /\n00:29 3 \u00b7 ASSERT: / B C / = / F G /, / F G / = / E H / \u2192 / B C / = / E H /\n00:38 4 \u00b7 ASSERT: / B C / = / E H /, / B C / \u2225 / E H / \u2192 / E B / = / H C /, / E B / \u2225 / H C / \u2192 \u27e8 E B C H \u27e9\n00:52 5 \u00b7 ASSERT: \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9 = \u27e8 E B C H \u27e9, \u27e8 E F G H \u27e9 = \u27e8 E B C H \u27e9\n01:06 6 \u00b7 \u2234: \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9 = \u27e8 E B C H \u27e9, \u27e8 E F G H \u27e9 = \u27e8 E B C H \u27e9 \u2192 \u27e8 A B C D \u27e9 = \u27e8 E F G H \u27e9\n\nGEOMETOR \u2022 G.65 \u2022 v2",
